From a0cd0f3219f2c3441603756f782b03717742e7cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 15:12:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sessions): a failed automation turn gets one delayed
 replay and says so, never 'send it again' [daveey]

A Kanban notice or background-job report turn that failed after its notice row
was written ended on the user-turn boundary "Your request was not processed.
Send it again ..." that nobody typed, and nothing ran it: the notice ledger acks
a notice once its row is in the transcript, and the refused-turn replay
(2185d7299c) excludes automation turns. 19 such rows on David-MBP in 4 days;
owner-wake, sweep-wake and chat close-out build failures (no Opus route under
quota) were dropped
the same way.

tui_gateway/automation_replay.py owns one bounded replay per chat:
- a failed kanban_notice/process_complete turn, or a wake whose agent build
  failed (owner-wake, sweep-wake, close-out), schedules ONE replay >= 60 s later, or at the
  recorded failure_resets_at for a typed quota/route exhaustion;
- newer failures in the same chat join the pending replay (one timer);
- a later successful turn cancels it when the delivery is in the transcript;
- the replay is marked; its own failure gives up and schedules nothing.
The anti-loop intent of 2185d7299c stays: automation turns still never get the
user-turn marker, and the replay is at most once.

The failed-turn boundary of an automation turn now says what failed and what
happens next ("Couldn't process the notice for t_...: <cause>. Retrying once at
HH:MM PT." / "Gave up after one retry."), via an agent copy hook in
_close_durable_failed_turn. A wake also restarts an already-failed agent build,
as prompt.submit does, so the replay does not re-read a stale agent_error.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
